{% call note("info", "Good to know", "Keep the comparison meaningful") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use a file you know is already on the computer; a cloud-only file would introduce another online step. You do not need to disconnect the internet or open a private document to make these notes. A comparison helps describe the experience; it does not rule out multiple problems.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="computer"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>If the delay starts on the computer</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Microsoft identifies limited storage, background startup apps, outdated software and older hardware among possible contributors to poor Windows performance. Closing unused apps and restarting are among its suggestions. Save your work before an ordinary restart and do not interrupt an update. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/performance-optimization/tips-to-improve-pc-performance-in-windows">Read Microsoft's Windows performance guidance</a>.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the main wait happens at startup, use our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://nakedtech.au/guides/computer-slow-startup/">slow-startup guide</a> to distinguish the stages. You do not need to disable unfamiliar software, delete files or install a “speed booster” to prepare useful notes.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="online"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>If the delay is mainly online</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Try another familiar online activity, and note whether another device on the same home Wi-Fi has similar trouble. A working connection can still leave a particular app or website with a problem. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/connectivity-networking/fix-wi-fi-connection-issues-in-windows">Microsoft's connection troubleshooting</a> includes checking a second device.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Record the room and time as well. If you make speed comparisons, nbn describes checking beside the router and in other rooms, with a wired comparison where practical. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://www.nbnco.com.au/learn/optimisation/what-to-look-for-in-a-wifi-router">See nbn's guidance</a>. One result is a reason to investigate, not a purchase recommendation.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/wifi-dropouts-diagnosis/">Wi-Fi dropout guide</a> includes a comparison table and a short symptom diary you can use.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="notes"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Turn the observation into a useful question</h2>
{% call note("info", "Good to know", "An example observation") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For example, you might write: “Opening a file already on this laptop feels normal, but the video call pauses in the study. I have not checked another device.” This is an invented example of a useful description, not a customer case or diagnosis.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Say what you have not checked") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Add when it started and anything that changed around that time. Say what you have not checked. If important files are inaccessible or the computer will not start, explain that before arranging a routine assessment; do not reset it to complete this checklist.</p>{% endcall %}

